Thanks all. Writing down what we know so far, proper RCA to follow.

What happened: A flash sale sent four times the normal order volume. Two work=
ers could not keep up and the orders topic built a backlog of 52,000 messages=
. Orders were taken but confirmed up to 25 minutes late.
Impact: No downtime. Confirmations were up to 25 minutes late for about 9,000=
 orders. No orders were lost and no SLA was breached.

Timeline (UTC):
2025-08-15 18:00 Flash sale started. None. The sale was not on the capacity c=
alendar.
2025-08-15 18:09 Alert OrderQueueConsumerLagHigh fired with lag at 14,000. On=
-call opened an incident and followed SOP-QUEUE-001.
2025-08-15 18:15 Workers restarted. Lag kept growing. Asked the orders team f=
or help.
2025-08-15 18:22 Orders team joined. Scaled orders-worker from 2 to 4 replica=
s.
2025-08-15 18:47 Lag back under 1,000. Closed the incident.

Root cause: Worker capacity was fixed at normal traffic levels and the sale w=
as not planned for. The lag procedure in use restarted workers, which added n=
o capacity.
Fix: Scaled orders-worker from 2 to 4 replicas. Scaled back to 2 the next mor=
ning.

Follow ups:
- Replace SOP-QUEUE-001 with a procedure that scales consumers. (Luis Romero)
- Add sales events to the capacity calendar. (Marketing team)
- Autoscale workers on consumer lag. (Orders team)

